  "panelHTML": "<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 28px;\"><div><b>CMDP view</b> (cost = violating steps): analytical E[N] &asymp; <b>positive, below the double-precision range</b> &nbsp;|&nbsp; sample mean 0.000 &plusmn; 0.000 &nbsp;|&nbsp; budget d = 0.0 &nbsp;<span style=\"display:inline-block;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:10px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;background:#c62828;\">FAILS</span> <span style=\"color:#888;\">(d = 0 demands N = 0 almost surely; with &sigma; &gt; 0 every step violates with positive probability, so E[N] &gt; 0 and the budget fails)</span></div><div><b>Chance view</b>: P(any violation in the episode) &asymp; <b>0.000</b> &plusmn; 0.000 (estimate) &nbsp;|&nbsp; level &delta; = 0.05 &nbsp;<span style=\"display:inline-block;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:10px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;\">SAMPLE PASSES</span></div><div><b>Risk view</b>: VaR<sub>&alpha;</sub>(Z) = -0.789, <b>CVaR<sub>&alpha;</sub>(Z) = -0.782</b> (mean of the worst 10% of the 200 sampled excursions; must be &le; 0) &nbsp;<span style=\"display:inline-block;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:10px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;\">SAMPLE PASSES</span></div><div><b>Hard view</b>: worst sampled excursion max Z = <b>-0.771</b> (must be &le; 0 in every episode) &nbsp;<span style=\"display:inline-block;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:10px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;\">SAMPLE PASSES</span> <span style=\"color:#888;\">&mdash; with Gaussian noise the true probability of ever violating is positive, so \"almost surely safe\" can never hold; 200 clean samples are not a proof.</span></div><div style=\"color:#555;\">Analytic: stationary sd &sigma;<sub>&infin;</sub> = &sigma;/&radic;(k(2&minus;k)) = 0.0320, stationary per-step violation probability p<sub>&infin;</sub> = 1 &minus; &Phi;((1 &minus; 0.8)/&sigma;<sub>&infin;</sub>) = 2.12e-10; Markov bound on the chance view: P &le; E[N] = positive, below the double-precision range.</div></div>",
  "conclusion": "All five actual binary64 marginal tails and their sum underflow to 0, while positive sigma implies positive true tails. The existing explicit zero-budget guard correctly fails and the display reports positivity below double precision.",
  "noBrowserOrFormalNumericProof": true
